<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oxfordshire</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oxfordshire is a county in south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, with its county town at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxford">Oxford</a>. Its western part, reaching into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotswolds">Cotswolds</a>, lay on the eastern edge of the territory of the Dobunni in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a>, and in the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a> it was a borderland between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a> and Mercia. It is home to the University of Oxford and to Blenheim Palace.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oxfordshire.jpg" alt="Oxfordshire" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dave Price · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_Islip,_Oxfordshire_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3892478_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
